        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continuousAt_def'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousAt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tendsto</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">𝓝</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">𝓝</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Iff</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This is a piece of <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/36769\">#36769</a> that we found useful, I'm actually very suprised this never existed before and the current <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=continuousAt_def#doc\">docs#continuousAt_def</a> is <em>not</em> hot <code>continuousAt</code> is defined! Should we (open another separate PR) and add this lemma?</p>",
